    <div class="home-section">
        <h2>Features</h2>
        <p>
            Planned demo/proof-of-concept features:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>☑ HTML UI on localhost</li>
            <li>☐ See list of documents in a simple log</li>
            <li>☐ Add new documents</li>
            <li>☐ Derive relationships between documents, thus storing a basic concept graph</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Planned minimum-viable-product features:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>☐ Registration flow</li>
            <li>☐ Security of logins and stored documents</li>
            <li>☐ Document editing, revision tracking, and synchronization</li>
            <li>☐ Shared graph database that can be queried and referenced in documents</li>
            <li>☐ Keyword search</li>
            <li>☐ Subscription service</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Some aspirational future features:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>☐ Collaborative real-time document editing</li>
            <li>☐ Deterministic document rendering</li>
            <li>☐ Document interactivity</li>
            <li>☐ Browser extension for embedding documents in other web pages</li>
            <li>☐ Multimedia elements in documents</li>
            <li>☐ Features for business</li>
            <li>☐ Desktop UI</li>
            <li>☐ Boot to Collective Toolbox</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="home-section">
        <h2>Project structure</h2>
        <p>
            The Collective Toolbox is <a href="https://www.fsf.org/about/what-is-free-software" target="_blank"
                class="link-external">free software</a>: free as in freedom, meaning you may study it or modify it. See
            the license terms (AGPL-3+ and others) in <a href="/src.tar.gz" class="link-download">the source code</a> (tar.gz
            download) for details.
        </p>
        <p>
            It is intended for use with a paid subscription service. The subscription will cover:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Hosted instance of the Collective Toolbox, so you can access it from anywhere</li>
            <li>Remote backup of your data</li>
            <li>Cloud synchronization</li>
            <li>Network services needed to use Collective Toolbox through Web browsers</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Terms of service for the subscription service will have some additional requirements specific to the
            service, outside of the software license terms.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="home-section">
        <h2>Pricing and Finances</h2>
        <p>
            This is meant to become a moderately-priced subscription service. Once development is further along, I'll
            evaulate what pricing will allow a sustainable profit margin to allow a degree of assurance in the project's
            future. Ideally, this would be somewhere in the area of $1 to $5 per month for typical use by a single
            person.
        </p>
        <p>
            I don't want some users to end up subsidizing others, since it doesn't seem sustainable or equitable.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>